      "title": "Preserve remembered UID/start identity before taking the normal-effective-UID path",
      "finding": "The saved-helper UID/start comparison exists only inside row[2] != os.geteuid(). A remembered privileged /bin/ps PID later observed with the current effective UID bypasses that comparison and line110 replaces known[pid], including its effective UID and start time. remaining() calls remember() first and then compares against the newly overwritten identity, so this transition/reuse is not rejected. A repeated /bin/ps kernel/file binding does not recover the original UID/start binding. Normal remembered descendants also have their start identity overwritten on each owned snapshot.",
      "static_counterexample": "Remember H with ruid=501,euid=0,start=A and a valid direct-wrapper ps role; observe the same H as a current-UID descendant with ruid=501,euid=501,start=B. The effective-UID exception branch is skipped, known[H] is rewritten to B, and the subsequent saved identity equality sees B rather than A. No reviewed code was executed.",
      "consequence": "The promised immutable owned-PID UID/start guard can silently accept a changed role/start and can make later per-PID cleanup checks use a replacement identity rather than the original owned instance.",
      "requested_correction": "Validate every already-known PID UID/start tuple before overwriting known, independently of current effective UID. Preserve the initially verified helper identity; allow only explicitly specified exit-display changes. Include the helper-to-normal-UID/start-change transition in bounded adverse evidence.",
      "regression_evidence_gap": "The recorded reused-helper-start case exercises the privileged-helper branch; no helper-to-normal-effective-UID case is listed."
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "severity": "P2",
      "path": "<repo>/.paperclip/worktrees/TJS-1882-meownero-vanguard-cross-platform-tester-binaries-and-verified-group-download-packages/build/tjs1882-3175-native-ci-payload07/vanguard/run-portable-ci.py",
      "line": 77,
      "related_lines": [
        80,
        82,
        83,
        94,
        98,
        110
      ],
      "title": "Reject unverified first-seen zombies rather than bypassing helper verification",
      "finding": "The zombie branch returns False for any first-seen owned row with the current real UID. It runs before effective-UID, helper role/arguments, kernel path, or root-owned SUID file binding validation. If pid is not in known, even euid=0 or another foreign effective UID is ignored and never added to known/cleanup evidence. This is broader than the documented already-verified helper exit/zombie allowance.",
      "static_counterexample": "An owned first-seen row with ruid=501,euid=99,state=Z and any command passes the real-UID check, has no known identity to compare, and returns False before EFFECTIVE_UID_NOT_ALLOWLISTED or helper_binding can run. No reviewed code was executed.",
      "consequence": "An unknown foreign-effective-UID or unverified privileged descendant can be silently omitted while supervision and known-PID cleanup still pass, violating the explicit fail-closed observer requirement.",
      "requested_correction": "Restrict relaxed zombie handling to a previously verified, unchanged UID/start identity. First-seen/unverified foreign-UID zombies must prevent a PASS and remain visible in sanitized failure evidence. Add an unknown-zombie/foreign-effective-UID case.",
      "regression_evidence_gap": "The recorded known-zombie and zombie-reused-start cases do not cover an unregistered zombie."
    }
  ],
